  "content": {
    "component": "news_article",
    "_uid": "1247-root",
    "title": "Choosing preventive medicine",
    "subtitle": null,
    "summary": "Alumnus Dr Taha Sabri on why he choose public health as his career.  ",
    "media": [
      {
        "_uid": "b78158ca10c452b1",
        "component": "news_media",
        "role": "banner",
        "filename": "1247-BannerImage.jpg",
        "src": "/news-media/1247-BannerImage.jpg",
        "media_type": "image",
        "caption": null,
        "alt": "Choosing preventive medicine"
      },
      {
        "_uid": "f4df803a295a5cee",
        "component": "news_media",
        "role": "medium",
        "filename": "1247-MediumImage.jpg",
        "src": "/news-media/1247-MediumImage.jpg",
        "media_type": "image",
        "caption": "Dr Taha Sabri (extreme left) seated with the audience during a health awareness session.",
        "alt": "Choosing preventive medicine"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The last two years of medical school are when students face important choices about their career. The majority of students choose to pursue a specialised field of medicine but even though Taha Sabri, MBBS '14, was keen on a clinical career in psychiatry, he ended up making a very unconventional choice."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "His decision was made in the backdrop of one of the worst terrorist incidents to hit his hometown of Karachi: the March 2013 Abbas Town blast which claimed over 40 lives. Jolted by the scale of the tragedy, Taha and his fellow AKU students organised a number of emergency medical camps in the area. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In the midst of the relief efforts, Taha noticed a wide range of conditions that could have been addressed through basic health awareness sessions, first-aid and commonly available medicines. He also noted a 'hidden burden' of mental health issues that needed to be addressed but the survivors were not aware of where to seek treatment."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Taha was moved by what he witnessed in Abbas Town and decided to focus on preventive healthcare by setting up his own NGO, the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Humanity Initiative",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "http://www.humanityinitiative.org/",
                    "target": "_blank",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " (HI). "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "HI brings together volunteer doctors from across Karachi to conduct health screening drives, medical camps and health education sessions in areas with the greatest need. The autonomous, student-run organisation now has over 300 volunteers and since 2013 has served over 5,000 people through medical camps and provided 8,000 people with health education training. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "HI has also trained over 1,000 people in disaster response and first aid, and a further 1,500 people in CPR, providing the hope of saving lives."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "He says: \"Our goal is to serve communities through preventive medicine. By focussing on simple, high value interventions we are able to promptly treat and thereby pre-empt the onset of many common diseases and conditions. All our efforts are on a volunteer basis and by taking young doctors to communities we hope to remind them of the humanitarian roots of their profession and to improve access to basic healthcare.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Taha is also keen to form partnerships that can help him scale up HI's community initiatives. In January 2015, he collaborated with the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Pakistan Association of Mental Health",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "https://www.facebook.com/PAMH.org.pk/",
                    "target": "_blank",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "CareForHealth",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "http://careforhealth.co/",
                    "target": "_blank",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " to set up "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Taskeen",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "http://taskeen.org/",
                    "target": "_blank",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " (solace) to combat stigmas about mental health."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "He is currently pursuing a Master's in Public Health at the University of Washington in Seattle on a Fulbright Scholarship and plans to return to Pakistan upon the completion of his degree. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\"My team members in Pakistan are managing HI in my absence. I am currently studying how developing countries can scale up high-impact interventions in the area of preventive healthcare and I can't wait to put this knowledge to use when I complete my degree,\" Taha added. "
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
